  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef owns several pairs of shoes, unfortunately he has so many that he lost track of them!\n\nEach pair of shoes consists of one left shoe and one right shoe.\n\nLooking at his collection, Chef counts LLL left shoes and RRR right shoes.\n\nWhat's the minimum number of shoes Chef is missing?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line of input will contain two space-separated integers LLL and RRR – the number of left shoes and right shoes, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a single integer: the minimum number of shoes Chef is missing.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤L,R≤101 \\leq L, R \\leq 101≤L,R≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 3",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere's one left shoe and three right shoes.\nThe single left shoe can be paired with one right shoe, leaving two unpaired right shoes. So, the answer is 222."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5 5",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are an equal number of left and right shoes, so it's possible to pair them all up."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "8 3",
        "output": "5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are 888 left shoes and 333 right shoes.\nEach right shoe can be paired up with one left shoe, which leaves 555 left shoes unpaired."
      }
    ]
  },
